#: NAVIGATION.md:1
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概要"

#: NAVIGATION.md:3
msgid ""
"A tutorial to run simple surface binding calculations using Metadynamics "
"through PLUMED. The procedure described herein is an extension of the "
"[earlier work of Doudou <em>et "
"al.</em>](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26609600/) (1) where the binding "
"free energy of a model binding system (and a benzamidine−trypsin system) are"
" calculated from a one-dimensional PMF and standardised to a reference state"
" of a 1 M solution. This procedure has been used extensively by our group "
"for binding processes on surfaces of "
"[halite](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/full/10.1021/acs.jctc.2c00787) (2) and "
"[calcite](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/full/10.1021/acs.jpcc.3c02864) (3)."
msgstr ""
"PLUMED の Metadynamics で簡単な表面結合を計算する Tutorial です。[Doudou "
"らの研究](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26609600/) (1) を拡張します。原著では、モデル系と "
"Benzamidine–Trypsin 系の結合自由エネルギーを1次元 PMF から求め、1 M の参照状態に標準化します。本手順は私たちの Group"
" で [Halite](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/full/10.1021/acs.jctc.2c00787) "
"(2)、[Calcite](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/full/10.1021/acs.jpcc.3c02864) (3) "
"表面の結合に広く使われています。"

#: NAVIGATION.md:5
msgid ""
"A harmonic restraint is applied to the binding atom orthogonal to the "
"collective variable used to describe the binding process. This has the "
"effect of constraining the binding atom to a cylindrical volume orthogonal "
"to the surface of interest. Equations 8 and 9 from the original paper of "
"Doudou <em>et al.</em> demonstrate that the volume explored in the unbound "
"region by the restrained binding atom can be analytically calculated and "
"referenced to the standard-state volume, producing a volumed-based free "
"energy correction to be applied to the total binding energy."
msgstr ""
"結合原子に、結合過程の CV と直交する Harmonic Restraint を加え、表面に垂直な円柱体積に制限します。Doudou "
"らの式8・9は、非結合領域で原子が探索する体積を解析的に求め、標準状態体積を参照して、全結合自由エネルギーに体積補正を加えられることを示します。"

#: NAVIGATION.md:7
msgid ""
"While the original paper allows for the correction of a harmonic restraint "
"with any spring constant, this method will only ever produce an upper limit "
"for any free energy barriers separating the bound and unbound regions due to"
" being forced to follow a straight path during separation. Here we describe "
"how to apply and account for a flat-bottomed cylindrical restraint with "
"harmonic walls starting at a specified radius instead of the harmonic "
"restraint used in the original paper, which represents the limiting case of "
"the general approach as the cylinder radius tends to zero. The flat-bottomed"
" restraint provides a region unperturbed by any harmonic potential, allowing"
" for the possibility of producing the actual free energy profile with "
"accurate barrier heights, for a sufficiently large radius value, which could"
" then be used for kinetic studies. Described [here](markdown/theory.md) are "
"the integrals for the flat-bottomed potentials and a brief overview on how "
"to turn the one-dimensional PMF into a standard binding free energy."
msgstr ""
"原著は任意の Spring Constant の補正を扱えますが、解離時に直線 Path を強制するため、結合・非結合領域間の Barrier "
"の上限しか得られません。ここでは、指定半径の外から Harmonic Wall が働く Flat-bottom 円柱 Restraint "
"の導入と補正を説明します。原著は半径0の極限です。Flat-bottom は Potential に乱されない領域を作り、十分大きな半径なら正しい "
"Barrier の Profile を得て Kinetics に使える可能性があります。[こちら](markdown/theory.md) "
"で積分と1次元 PMF から標準結合自由エネルギーへの変換を説明します。"

#: NAVIGATION.md:9
msgid "System creation"
msgstr "系の作成"

#: NAVIGATION.md:11
msgid ""
"For this tutorial, we have constructed a simple model system that will run "
"and converge quickly on any machine while still mimicking the important "
"aspects of an actual binding profile. The details on how this has been done "
"are presented [here](markdown/system.md)."
msgstr ""
"実際の結合 Profile の重要部分を再現しながら、どのマシンでも速く実行・収束する簡単なモデルを作りました。詳細は "
"[こちら](markdown/system.md) です。"

#: NAVIGATION.md:13
msgid "Input files & running simulation"
msgstr "入力ファイルと実行"

#: NAVIGATION.md:15
msgid ""
"[OpenMM](https://github.com/openmm/openmm) (4) has been chosen as the "
"molecular dynamics engine for this tutorial, utilising PLUMED through the "
"[openmm-plumed plugin](https://github.com/openmm/openmm-plumed). Details on "
"the input files provided, their meaning, and how to use them are discussed "
"[here](markdown/inputs.md)."
msgstr ""
"MD エンジンは [OpenMM](https://github.com/openmm/openmm) (4)、PLUMED 連携は [openmm-"
"plumed Plugin](https://github.com/openmm/openmm-plumed) を使います。入力の内容と使い方は "
"[こちら](markdown/inputs.md) です。"

#: NAVIGATION.md:17
msgid "Analysing simulation"
msgstr "シミュレーションの解析"

#: NAVIGATION.md:19
msgid ""
"Using the PLUMED command line tool and a series of Python and bash scripts, "
"we demonstrate how to analyse the raw HILLS file produced by these "
"simulations and generate the final standard binding free energies. All "
"details can be found [here](markdown/analysis.md)."
msgstr ""
"PLUMED のコマンドラインと Python・Bash で HILLS を解析し、最終的な標準結合自由エネルギーを求めます。詳細は "
"[こちら](markdown/analysis.md) です。"

